---
import LessonPage from "../../../components/lesson/LessonPage.astro";
import { defineLesson } from "../../../data/lesson-schema.mjs";
export const page = defineLesson({
  "title": "Adverbs of manner · A2 Grammar · Curriculum Map",
  "slug": "adverbs-of-manner",
  "level": "A2",
  "topic": "Adverbs of manner",
  "category": "Grammar",
  "contentType": "grammar",
  "status": "ready",
  "description": "Describe how people do things. Build natural sentences like She explains everything clearly , He drives carefully , They work hard , and She speaks English well.",
  "sequence": 10,
  "prerequisites": [],
  "related": [],
  "assessments": [
    "a2-exit"
  ]
});
---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 10</p>
  <h1>Adverbs of manner <em>-ly</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Describe how people do things. Build natural sentences like <span class="ex">She explains everything clearly</span>, <span class="ex">He drives carefully</span>, <span class="ex">They work hard</span>, and <span class="ex">She speaks English well.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 55–65 min</span>
    <span class="tag">how actions happen</span>
    <span class="tag">slowly · carefully · well</span>
    <span class="tag">adjective vs adverb</span>
    <span class="tag">11 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Compare a careful driver with drives carefully.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Turn adjectives into how-words with -ly.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Choose, spell, and place adverbs; repair classic errors.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Describe how you really do things at work and home.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Adverbs of manner answer one question about the action: <span class="ex">How?</span> One small ending, <span class="ex">-ly</span>, moves your English from what you do to how you do it.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="faster">faster</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="fastest">fastest</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="careful">careful</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="carefully">carefully</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="never">never</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="always">always</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The metro is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="faster" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> than the bus. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(comparatives, A2 Lesson 5)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>She is a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="careful" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> driver. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(adjectives, A1)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="never" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> drinks coffee at night, so he sleeps well. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(adverbs of frequency, A1)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Two sentences about the same person</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"Marta is a careful driver. She drives carefully."</span><br /><span class="ex">"Tomás is a quick learner. He learns quickly."</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which word describes the person: <span class="ex">careful</span> or <span class="ex">carefully</span>?</li>
      <li>Which word describes the action of driving?</li>
      <li>What two letters appear at the end of <span class="ex">carefully</span> and <span class="ex">quickly</span>?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check: thing or action?</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">If the word describes a person or thing, choose the adjective. If it describes the action, choose the <b>-ly</b> word.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="slow">slow</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="slowly">slowly</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="careful">careful</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="carefully">carefully</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="quiet">quiet</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="quietly">quietly</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The traffic is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="slow" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> in the morning, so I leave early.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The teacher speaks <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="slowly" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>, word by word.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>She is a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="careful" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> driver; she never gets tickets.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>She checks every document <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="carefully" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> before she sends it.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Please be <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="quiet" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> in the library.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The meeting is next door, so please talk <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="quietly" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: adjective + -ly</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Adjectives describe people and things. Adverbs of manner describe actions: they say <strong>how</strong> something happens. Most adverbs of manner are simply <span class="ex">adjective + -ly</span>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>adjective describes a thing</th><th>adverb describes the action</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>The traffic is <b>slow</b>.</td><td>He drives <b>slowly</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>She is a <b>careful</b> writer.</td><td>She writes <b>carefully</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Your voice is <b>quiet</b>.</td><td>You speak <b>quietly</b>.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Spelling changes you need</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>adjective ending</th><th>change</th><th>examples</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>most adjectives</td><td>add -ly</td><td><span class="contraction">slow → slowly, careful → carefully, clear → clearly</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>consonant + -y</td><td>-y becomes -ily</td><td><span class="contraction">happy → happily, easy → easily</span></td></tr>
        <tr><td>-le</td><td>-le becomes -ly</td><td><span class="contraction">terrible → terribly, gentle → gently</span></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: point at the action</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>An adjective points at a person or thing: in <span class="ex">a careful driver</span>, the word <span class="ex">careful</span> points at the driver. When you add <span class="ex">-ly</span>, the word turns and points at the action instead: in <span class="ex">She drives carefully</span>, the word <span class="ex">carefully</span> points at the driving. Nothing new is happening in the world; you are choosing what to describe.</p>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Follow where the word points</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">She is a clear speaker. → clear points at she.</span><br /><span class="ex">She speaks clearly. → clearly points at speaks.</span></p>
    <p>Ask <span class="ex">How does she speak?</span> and the answer is the adverb of manner: <span class="ex">clearly</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>Four adverbs refuse the -ly pattern</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>adjective</th><th>adverb of manner</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>good</b></td><td><b>well</b></td><td><span class="contraction">She plays the guitar well.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>fast</b></td><td><b>fast</b></td><td><span class="contraction">He talks fast.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>hard</b></td><td><b>hard</b></td><td><span class="contraction">They work hard.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>late</b></td><td><b>late</b></td><td><span class="contraction">The bus arrived late.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Careful: <span class="ex">hardly</span> and <span class="ex">lately</span> exist, but they are not the adverbs of <span class="ex">hard</span> and <span class="ex">late</span>. <span class="ex">Hardly</span> means almost not (<span class="ex">I hardly slept</span>), and <span class="ex">lately</span> means recently.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the right word</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">First decide: does the gap describe a thing or an action? Then choose.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="quickly">quickly</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="quiet">quiet</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="carefully">carefully</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="well">well</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="hard">hard</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="easily">easily</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="slow">slow</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="clearly">clearly</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The ambulance arrived <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="quickly" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>, in only four minutes.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Our street is very <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="quiet" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at night.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Read the contract <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="carefully" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> before you sign it.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>He did <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="well" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on his driving test.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>She worked <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="hard" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> all weekend to finish the report.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>I get lost <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="easily" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> in new cities.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The Wi-Fi is really <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="slow" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> today.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>Please speak <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="clearly" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> into the microphone so everyone understands you.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Where does the adverb go?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Adverbs of manner usually come after the verb, and after its object if there is one. Keep the verb and its object together; the how-word waits until the end.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>say</th><th>do not say</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>She speaks <b>English clearly</b>.</td><td>She speaks clearly English.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>I read <b>the contract carefully</b>.</td><td>I read carefully the contract.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Compare with adverbs of frequency from A1: <span class="ex">always</span>, <span class="ex">usually</span>, and <span class="ex">never</span> go before the main verb, but adverbs of manner go after it: <span class="ex">She always answers clearly.</span></p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>After be, look, sound, and feel, use the adjective</h3>
    <p>These verbs do not describe an action; they describe the thing itself. Say <span class="ex">The plan looks good</span>, not <span class="ex">The plan looks well</span>. Say <span class="ex">That sounds great</span> and <span class="ex">I feel bad about the delay</span>. No <span class="ex">-ly</span> is needed, because nothing is being done.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-answer-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2: type the adverb of manner</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Build the adverb from the adjective in parentheses. Watch the spelling rules, and remember the irregulars.</p>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>She answered every question <input class="answer-input" data-answer="clearly" aria-label="answer 1" />. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(clear)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>We found the office <input class="answer-input" data-answer="easily" aria-label="answer 2" />. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(easy)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Close the laptop <input class="answer-input" data-answer="gently" aria-label="answer 3" />. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(gentle)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Please pack the glasses <input class="answer-input" data-answer="carefully" aria-label="answer 4" />. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(careful)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>She speaks Portuguese very <input class="answer-input" data-answer="well" aria-label="answer 5" />. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(good)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>He works <input class="answer-input" data-answer="hard" aria-label="answer 6" /> every day. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(hard)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-answers>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-answers>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A team note about a new colleague</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"Elena joined our support team in April, and the first results look good. She learns quickly and explains technical problems clearly, so customers trust her. She never arrives late, and she works hard, even on busy days. She still answers some messages slowly, because she checks every detail carefully. That is fine; speed will come with practice."</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You followed how, not just what, in a real workplace note.">
    <h3>Drill 3: read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="She explains technical problems clearly.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. Why do customers trust Elena?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She explains technical problems clearly.">She explains technical problems clearly.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She answers every message quickly.">She answers every message quickly.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She arrives before everyone else.">She arrives before everyone else.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="She checks every detail carefully.">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. Why does Elena answer some messages slowly?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She checks every detail carefully.">She checks every detail carefully.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She is still learning to type.">She is still learning to type.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She arrives late on busy days.">She arrives late on busy days.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="She works hard, even on busy days.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. Which sentence about Elena is true?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She works hard, even on busy days.">She works hard, even on busy days.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She often arrives late.">She often arrives late.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="She learns slowly.">She learns slowly.</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="she speaks english very clearly">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the sentence</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Build the sentence. Keep the verb and its object together; the adverb comes last.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="english">English</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="she">She</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="clearly">clearly</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="speaks">speaks</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="very">very</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="he plays the guitar well">
    <h3>Drill 5: build with an irregular adverb</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Build the sentence. The adverb of good goes after the object.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="guitar">guitar</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="well">well</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="he">He</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="plays">plays</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="careful" data-fix="He drives very carefully at night." data-why="Careful is an adjective, so it describes a thing. The action drives needs the adverb carefully.">
    <h3>Drill 6: describe the action</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="he">He</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="drives">drives</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="very">very</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="careful">careful</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="night">at night.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="good" data-fix="The team played very well yesterday." data-why="Good is an adjective. After an action verb like played, use the irregular adverb well.">
    <h3>Drill 7: the good / well trap</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="team">The team</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="played">played</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="very">very</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="good">good</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="yesterday">yesterday.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 8: say it, then reveal</h3>
    <p>Read the cue, say the full sentence aloud, then reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> She is a careful driver. Say it with drives.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>She drives carefully.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> He is a quick learner. Say it with learns.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He learns quickly.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> They are good singers. Say it with sing.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>They sing well.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> He is a hard worker. Say it with works.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He works hard.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> I am a slow reader. Say it with read.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>I read slowly.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> The plan is good. Say it with looks.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The plan looks good.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your work style:</b> Say four true sentences about how you do things at work or at home. <span class="ex">I answer messages quickly. I cook slowly but well.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Ask the teacher:</b> Ask three questions about how your teacher does things, then react to the answers. <span class="ex">Do you drive carefully? Do you cook well?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Someone you respect:</b> Describe how a coworker, friend, or family member does things. <span class="ex">My sister explains problems clearly. She never gives up easily.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Honest confessions:</b> Say three things you do slowly or not very well. <span class="ex">I park slowly. I don’t sing well.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Same and different:</b> Compare how you and another person do the same task. <span class="ex">We both work hard. He types fast, but I type slowly.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the system back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “Adjectives describe ______. Adverbs of manner describe ______ and usually end in ______. The adverb of good is ______. Fast, hard, and late do not ______. After verbs like be, look, and feel, I use the ______.”</p>
    <p>Then describe how you did three real things this week: one thing you did well, one thing you did quickly, and one thing you did carefully.</p>
